            <title>[LU-21123] obdclass: uninitialized remainder in percent size parsing</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21123</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;sysfs_memparse_total()&lt;/tt&gt; can return a wrong size for a percentage with a zero integer part, such as &lt;tt&gt;0%&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;0.5%&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;.5%&lt;/tt&gt;. The result depends on stack contents.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Cause"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Cause&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;scale64_rem()&lt;/tt&gt; returns early for a zero base and does not set &lt;tt&gt;*remp&lt;/tt&gt;. &lt;tt&gt;__string_to_size()&lt;/tt&gt; then adds this uninitialized remainder before it divides by 100.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Commit &lt;tt&gt;f62e51414712&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18163" class="external-link" rel="nofollow"&gt;LU-18163&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/56334" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;review 56334&lt;/a&gt;) added this caller. It is in master since 2.16.51 and in 2.17.0.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Impact"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Impact&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;llite &lt;tt&gt;max_read_ahead_mb&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;max_read_ahead_per_file_mb&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;max_read_ahead_whole_mb&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;max_cached_mb&lt;/tt&gt;, and lod &lt;tt&gt;dom_threshold_free_mb&lt;/tt&gt;, accept these percentages.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;obd_init_checks()&lt;/tt&gt; parses &lt;tt&gt;0%&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;0.5%&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;.5%&lt;/tt&gt; when obdclass loads. A stale value of 100 or more fails a check, and obdclass does not load.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Fix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Set &lt;tt&gt;*remp&lt;/tt&gt; to zero on the zero-base return. The existing &lt;tt&gt;obd_init_checks()&lt;/tt&gt; cases cover these inputs. A new test cannot force the stale value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Found while adding percentage support to &lt;tt&gt;client_jobstats_max_memory&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21060" class="external-link" rel="nofollow"&gt;LU-21060&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
